      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Okay so me and KaaneWolf discovered that users that have vrcx running on launch have been having this issue and when we both decided to not have vrcx launched when booting vrchat it fixed the issue. We dont know why or how but wee tested it 10 times without vrcx and 10 times with vrcx and every single time it worked without vrcx launch when you first boot vrchat. This may not be the solution for everyone but it worked for me and Kaane. I hope this helps but it could still absolutely be a bug with steamvr or even vrcx or both.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-07-02T19:23:47.098Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Yesterday in Open-Beta and today in Unity 6 Beta the first time I open up and login to  VRChat it fails to load and turns black. Once I close the application and reopen VRChat it runs normally. I think there may be a bug or most likely a memory leak issue. After looking at my log, during initial start up I did get:\n\nNullReferenceException after entering my home world at start up.\n\nThe world hasn't been updated in some time and has perfectly loaded before. So is this a VRChat-Client Side issue?",
